#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 194
#: rc.cpp:1267
msgid ""
"Isobars are nuclides having the same mass number, i.e. sum of protons plus "
"neutrons."
msgstr ""
"দু'টি নিউক্লিড-এর ভর সংখ্যা সমান হলে, অর্থাৎ প্রোটোন ও নিউট্রন সংখ্যা সমান হলে, "
"তাদেরকে আইসোবার বলা হয়।"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 203
#: rc.cpp:1282
msgid ""
"A nuclear isomer is a metastable or isomeric state of an atom caused by the "
"excitation of a proton or neutron in its nucleus so that it requires a "
"change in spin before it can release its extra energy. They decay to lower "
"energy states of the nuclide through two isomeric transitions:[br] -> "
"&#947;- emission (emission of a high-energy photon)[br] -> internal "
"conversion (the energy is used to ionize the atom)[br] Contrast this with "
"the definition of a chemical isomer, the more common use of the word. Also "
"contrast with the meaning of isotope, in which the difference is the number "
"of neutrons in the nucleus. Metastable isomers of a particular atom are "
"usually designated with an \"m\" (or, in the case of atoms with more than "
"one isomer, 2m, 3m, and so on). This designation is usually placed after the "
"atomic symbol and number of the atom (e.g., Co-58m), but is sometimes placed "
"as a superscript before (e.g., [sup]m[/sup]Co-58 or [sup]58m[/sup]Co)."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 211
#: rc.cpp:1294
msgid "Beta rays"
msgstr "বিটা রশ্মি"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 212
#: rc.cpp:1297
msgid ""
"Rays consisting of electrons that are emitted from Atoms of radioactive "
"elements."
msgstr "তেজস্ক্রিয় মৌল থেকে বিকিরিত এক প্রকার রশ্মি যা ইলেকট্রন দ্বারা গঠিত।"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 217
#: rc.cpp:1303
msgid ""
"The electron is a subatomic particle with a mass of m[sub]e[/sub]=(9.1093897 "
"&#177; 0.0000054)e-31 kg and a negative charge of [i]e[/i]=(1.60217733 "
"&#177; 0.00000049)e-19 C\n"
"\t\t"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 224
#: rc.cpp:1313
msgid ""
"The proton is a subatomic particle with a mass of m[sub]e[/sub]=(1.6726231 "
"&#177; 0.0000010) 10[sup]-27[/sup] kg and a positive charge of [i]e[/i]="
"(1.60217733 &#177; 0.00000049) 10[sup]-19[/sup] C which occurs in the "
"nucleus of an atom."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 233
#: rc.cpp:1328
msgid ""
"The neutron is a subatomic particle with a mass of m[sub]e[/sub]=(1.6749286 "
"&#177; 0.0000010) 10[sup]-27[/sup] kg which occurs in the nucleus of an atom."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 241
#: rc.cpp:1340
msgid "Cathode Rays"
msgstr "ক্যাথোড রশ্মি"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 242
#: rc.cpp:1343
msgid ""
"Cathode rays are streams of electrons observed in vacuum tubes, i.e. "
"evacuated glass tubes that are equipped with at least two electrodes, a "
"cathode (negative electrode) and an anode (positive electrode) in a "
"configuration known as a diode."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 248
#. i18n: tag refitem
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 262
#. i18n: tag refitem
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 271
#. i18n: tag refitem
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 279
#: rc.cpp:1349 rc.cpp:1376 rc.cpp:1391 rc.cpp:1403
msgid "Ionic Radius"
msgstr "আয়োনিক ব্যাসার্ধ"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 249
#: rc.cpp:1352
msgid ""
"The Ionic Radius is the radius of a charged atom, a so called ion. The ion "
"can have a positive or a negative charge. The charge of the ion which radius "
"you see is also displayed in Kalzium. A positive ion has less electrons in "
"its shell then the atom, a negative ion has more electrons. Therefore, a "
"postive ion has a smaller radius than its atom and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 258
#: rc.cpp:1367
msgid ""
"The van der Waals radius of an atom is the radius of an imaginary hard "
"sphere which can be used to model the atom for many purposes. Van der Waals "
"radii are determined from measurements of atomic spacing between pairs of "
"unbonded atoms in crystals."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 267
#: rc.cpp:1382
msgid ""
"The atomic radius is the distance from the atomic nucleus to the outmost "
"stable electron orbital in a atom that is at equilibrium."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/knowledge.xml line 276
#: rc.cpp:1397
msgid ""
"Covalent radius in chemistry corresponds to half of the distance between two "
"identical atomic nuclei, bound by a covalent bond."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 5
#: rc.cpp:1409
msgid "Watchglass"
msgstr "ওয়াচ-গ্লাস"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 6
#: rc.cpp:1412
msgid ""
"Watchglasses are round glass panes with a diameter of around 5 - 10 cm which "
"are used in the various experimental techniques. The border is bent upwards "
"to allow the watchglass to hold small amounts of liquids in order to let "
"them evaporate. The evaporation can be accelerated by heating the watchglass "
"with a Bunsen burner. Watchglasses can also be used to cover petri dishes or "
"beakers. Moreover watchglasses are suited to weighing small amounts of "
"matter or alternatively drying them in the airing cupboard. The term "
"watchglass is derived from the former pocket watches' protection glass which "
"was often domed."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 10
#: rc.cpp:1415
msgid "Dehydrator"
msgstr "শোষকাধার"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 13
#: rc.cpp:1418
msgid ""
"A dehydrator is a laboratory apparatus which is often made of glass and "
"serves to dry chemical matters, that is, to remove water or liquid from a "
"sample.\n"
"\t\t\tIn principle it is a glass bowl with cap which has a planar grinding "
"so that the bowl is air tight closeable. The dehydrator's lower part is "
"ordinarily filled with a drying agent e.g. calcium chloride, silica gel, "
"phosphoric anhydride or sulphuric acid. The sample to be dried is placed on "
"a diaphanous cartridge of plastic or ceramics above the drying agent.\n"
"\t\t\tThe drying agent is hygroscopic, which means that it dehumidifies its "
"environment by absorbing water vapor. The dry atmosphere then takes up water "
"from the sample to be dried."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 17
#: rc.cpp:1423
msgid "Spatula"
msgstr "স্প্যাচুলা"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 18
#: rc.cpp:1426
msgid ""
" The spatula is a laboratory tool to scrape off, grind and transport "
"chemicals. The material they are made of (e.g. iron, titanium, platinum) and "
"their design (e.g. flat spatula or spoon spatula) can be different."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 22
#: rc.cpp:1429
msgid "Water Jet Pump"
msgstr "পানি জেট পাম্প"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 23
#: rc.cpp:1432
msgid ""
"The water jet pump has two entry pipes and one exit and consists in "
"principle of two pipes one inside the other. At the water entry a water jet "
"shoots under full pressure out of a nozzle into a slightly larger pipe. "
"Thereby the water jet carries away air or fluid from the second entry. <br> "
"this is caused by the negative pressure in a drifting fluid. Thus it is an "
"application of the hydrodynamic paradox. This says that objects close to "
"drifting fluids are aspirated instead of being pushed away."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 27
#: rc.cpp:1435
msgid "Refractometer"
msgstr "প্রতিসরণ-পরিমাপক"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 28
#: rc.cpp:1438
msgid ""
"With a refractometer the refractive index of optical media is determined. If "
"the refractive index of a chemical is known it can be used after a synthesis "
"to determine the sample's purity or to audit the synthesis' success."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 32
#: rc.cpp:1441
#, fuzzy
msgid "Mortar"
msgstr "হামানদিস্তা"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 33
#: rc.cpp:1444
msgid ""
"A mortar is used for  manually grinding solids. It can also be used to "
"homogenize a mixture of powders by grinding. A club-shaped tool known as a "
"pestle is used with the mortar for grinding."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 37
#: rc.cpp:1447
msgid "Heating Coil"
msgstr "উত্তাপক কয়েল"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 38
#: rc.cpp:1450
msgid ""
"Heating coils are used to heat flasks and other containers. Multiple heating "
"coils can be connected with a thermometer so that the heat will not exceed a "
"specified temperature. It is possible to use a magnetic field inside the "
"heating coil to stir fluids with a magnetic stirrer. This will homogenize "
"the fluid in terms of temperature and composition."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 42
#: rc.cpp:1453
msgid "Cork Ring"
msgstr "কর্ক বলয়"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 43
#: rc.cpp:1456
msgid ""
"Large containers like round-bottomed flasks are placed on rings made of "
"cork, a special soft lightweight wood with good insulating qualities to "
"protect fragile instruments."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 47
#: rc.cpp:1459
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Separating Funnel"
msgid "Dropping Funnel"
msgstr "পৃথকীকরণ ফানেল"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 48
#: rc.cpp:1462
msgid ""
"A dropping funnel can be used to drop precise amounts of fluid. You can "
"control the dropping speed with a valve."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 52
#: rc.cpp:1465
msgid "Separating Funnel"
msgstr "পৃথকীকরণ ফানেল"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 53
#: rc.cpp:1468
msgid ""
"A separating funnel can be used to separate a mixture of fluids by differing "
"density. A valve at the bottom allows you to drain the more dense fluid for "
"transfer to another container."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 57
#: rc.cpp:1471
msgid "Test Tube Rack"
msgstr "টেস্ট টিউব ধারক"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 58
#: rc.cpp:1474
msgid ""
"This rack comes in handy when you want to test many small amounts of "
"chemicals in a row, or if you want to dry test tubes."
msgstr ""

# FIXME
#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 62
#: rc.cpp:1477
msgid "Vortexer"
msgstr "ভরটেক্সার"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 63
#: rc.cpp:1480
msgid ""
"A vortexer serves to homogenize reagents found in laboratories. The "
"container containing liquid to be homogenized is put on a platform. The "
"platform shakes by rotary agitation up to 3000RPM at which point a contact "
"sensor is activated. In this way extremely small volumes of fluid can be "
"homogenized quickly as well. It is the opposite of a centrifuge, used to "
"separate fluids."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 67
#: rc.cpp:1483
msgid "Wash Bottle"
msgstr "ওয়াশ বোতল"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 68
#: rc.cpp:1486
msgid ""
"These bottles are used for many purposes. In most laboratories they are "
"usually filled with water, salt, acid or other commonly used fluids. They "
"make it easy to apply the fluid if you do not need to measure a precise "
"amount."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 72
#: rc.cpp:1489
msgid "Rotary Evaporator"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 73
#: rc.cpp:1492
msgid ""
"A rotary evaporator consists of a round flask in a bath of hot water that is "
"designed to evaporate solvents. The flask is rotated and the solvent "
"collects under a vacuum onto a condenser and drips into a condensate "
"collecting flask. in this way solutions can be concentrated or purified. By "
"attaching a vacuum pump, the air pressure and therefore  the boiling point "
"of the fluid can be decreased."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 77
#: rc.cpp:1495
msgid "Reflux Condenser"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 78
#: rc.cpp:1498
msgid ""
"A reflux condenser subjects fluid to a process where a gas produced by "
"heating is collected on the reflux condenser. The fluid is cooled until it "
"condenses and runs back into the original fluid. Usually it is put on a "
"round-bottomed flask or several neck flasks."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 82
#: rc.cpp:1501
msgid "Pipette Bulb"
msgstr "পিপেট বাল্ব"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 83
#: rc.cpp:1504
msgid ""
"A pipette bulb is used to fill pipettes. It produces a negative pressure "
"which makes the fluid go into the pipette. If one lets air back into the "
"ball the fluid will run out of the pipette."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 87
#: rc.cpp:1507
msgid "Test Tube"
msgstr "টেস্ট টিউব"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 88
#: rc.cpp:1510
msgid ""
"In a test tube  small reactions or experiements are performed. There are "
"many different types of tubes. For example some have connectors, some are "
"etched for measurements, some are hardened for durability."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 92
#: rc.cpp:1513
msgid "Protective Goggles"
msgstr "নিরাপদ চশমা"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 93
#: rc.cpp:1516
msgid ""
"Most laboratories insist that everyone wears protective goggles. Without "
"them, it is too risky to work with most chemicals. Usually, the lens is a "
"special type of plastic which protects you from both mechanical impacts and "
"acid and base chemicals."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 97
#: rc.cpp:1519
msgid "Round-bottomed Flask"
msgstr "গোলতলী ফ্লাস্ক"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 98
#: rc.cpp:1522
msgid ""
"A round-bottomed flask is used for a lot of reactions. Some can be connected "
"to other items, as the frosting on the neck shows. With cork rings they can "
"be placed on a table."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 102
#: rc.cpp:1525
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Pipette"
msgid "Full Pipette"
msgstr "পিপেট"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 103
#: rc.cpp:1528
msgid ""
"Unlike a regular pipette, a full pipette only has one marking for a specific "
"volume."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 107
#: rc.cpp:1531
msgid "Drying Tube"
msgstr "নিরুদন টিউব"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 108
#: rc.cpp:1534
msgid ""
"There are reactions which need to be kept free of water. To make this "
"possible one uses a drying tube, which contains a hygroscopic chemical to "
"absorb water in the atmosphere."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 112
#: rc.cpp:1537
msgid "Test tube fastener"
msgstr "টেস্ট টিউব ধারক"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 113
#: rc.cpp:1540
msgid ""
"With a test tube fastener you can easily hold test tubes. If you use a "
"fastener there is a safe distance between the hand and the test tube when "
"the tube is hot. In particular, it is used when you hold a test tube over an "
"open flame."
msgstr ""

# FIXME
#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 117
#: rc.cpp:1543
msgid "Measuring Cylinder"
msgstr "মাপনী সিলিন্ডার"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 118
#: rc.cpp:1546
msgid ""
"In a measuring cylinder you can fill amounts of liquids relatively "
"precisely. Furthermore, the cylinder allows particulate matter to sink. "
"Following this, you can separate particulates from the fluid by decanting."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 122
#: rc.cpp:1549
msgid "Thermometer"
msgstr "থার্মোমিটার"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 123
#: rc.cpp:1552
msgid ""
"With a thermometer you can determine the temperature of a sample. In a "
"laboratory special thermometers are used, which can also be used within "
"acids or bases."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 127
#: rc.cpp:1555
msgid "Magnetic stir bar"
msgstr "চৌম্বক ঘূর্ণি দণ্ড"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 128
#: rc.cpp:1558
msgid ""
"Magnetic stir bars are highly chemically inert, small magnetic bars. Most "
"heaters have a built-in magnet which can rotate. This causes the stir bar to "
"rotate and the mixture to be homogenized."
msgstr ""

# FIXME
#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 132
#: rc.cpp:1561
msgid "Magnetic Stir Bar Retriever"
msgstr "চৌম্বক ঘূর্ণি দণ্ড উদ্ধারকারী"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 133
#: rc.cpp:1564
msgid ""
"With a magnetic stir bar retriever you can remove magnetic stir bars from a "
"container. The retriever is a bar with a magnet at the end which attracts "
"the stir bars."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 137
#: rc.cpp:1567
msgid "Pipette"
msgstr "পিপেট"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 138
#: rc.cpp:1570
msgid ""
"Pipettes are used to introduce small quantities of liquids in laboratories. "
"A pipette has a volume scale and as a rule pileusballs are used as droppers "
"for liquids. Both sorts of pipettes are calibrated for fluids with a "
"temperature of 20°C and for time of outflow (signified by \"Ex.\"). If "
"needed times of outflow are indicated on the pipettes."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 142
#: rc.cpp:1573
msgid "Erlenmeyer Flask"
msgstr "আর্লেনমায়ার ফ্লাস্ক"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 148
#: rc.cpp:1576
msgid ""
"This flask named after the chemist Emil Erlenmeyer (1825-1909) comes - "
"unlike the beaker - with an inverted conical base and a cylindrical neck. "
"There are different types of Erlenmeyer flasks for laboratory applications, "
"the narrow and wide neck form. Depending on the application the flask may "
"have precision grinding to allow good connection to other containers.\n"
"\t\t\t<br>\n"
"\t\t\tThe narrow neck reduces the risk of fluid escaping, especially when "
"boiling or during reactions which agitate the contents.\n"
"\t\t\t<br>\n"
"\t\t\tAn Erlenmeyer flask is useful for mixing fluids or accelerating "
"reactions by stirring or shaking, for example. The Erlenmeyer flask is "
"particularly suited for a magnetic stirrer, since it can be placed directly "
"on the stirring platform. A round-bottomed flask, by contrast, must be "
"placed on a cork ring on the stirring platform.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 153
#: rc.cpp:1584
msgid "Ultrasonic Bath"
msgstr "অতিশাব্দিক গোসল (bath)"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 154
#: rc.cpp:1587
msgid ""
"For some chemical reactions it is important that the solvent is gas free. To "
"achieve this the reaction vessel is put for some time into a ultrasonic "
"bath. Through the high sound frequency the vapor locks peel away and ascend. "
"This procedure is called outgassing."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 158
#: rc.cpp:1590
#, fuzzy
msgid "Scales"
msgstr "নিক্তি"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 159
#: rc.cpp:1593
msgid ""
"In a laboratory you often have to weigh out very precise amounts of "
"reagents. High precise scales can measure masses down to 1/10000 gram."
"Therefor they stand on granite blocks to avoid vibrancies and are protected "
"against blasts by a dome."
msgstr ""

# FIXME
#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 163
#: rc.cpp:1596
msgid "Distillation bridge"
msgstr "পাতন নল"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 164
#: rc.cpp:1599
msgid ""
"To separate a mixture you can use distillation amongst others. The "
"distillation bridge is thereby the way between the two pots. In the one pot "
"there is the mixture to be separated. Through heating, a gas forms which is "
"lead through the bridge. At the end of the bridge the gas phase is condensed "
"again and drips in a round flask. As a rule, the bridge is cooled by return "
"flow. In addition, there is often a thermometer for controlling the "
"temperature on the distillation bridge."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 169
#: rc.cpp:1602
msgid "Syringe"
msgstr "সিরিনজ"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 170
#: rc.cpp:1605
msgid ""
"A syringe consists of two parts: A glass tube and a punch. Both are normally "
"made of glass. A gas floats into the glass tube. As the syringe is a closed "
"system the punch has to give way. This can be used measuring the volume of "
"an reaction."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 174
#: rc.cpp:1608
msgid "Separation Beaker"
msgstr "পৃথকীকরণ বিকার"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 175
#: rc.cpp:1611
msgid ""
"At the four ends of this separation beaker you put four small caps. While "
"distilling, you can turn the beaker by 60 degree after a certain temperate "
"has been reached. This way, at the end of the distillation all four caps "
"have a specific liquid in it, depending on the boiling points of the liquid "
"distilled."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 179
#: rc.cpp:1614
msgid "Burner"
msgstr "দীপ"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 180
#: rc.cpp:1617
msgid ""
"There are several types of burners. The picture shows a Teclu-Burner. Each "
"type has specific uses. They vary in the peak temperature and overall "
"heating capability."
msgstr ""

# FIXME
#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 184
#: rc.cpp:1620
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Extraction"
msgid "Extractor Hood"
msgstr "আহরণ"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 185
#: rc.cpp:1623
msgid ""
"Most laboratories use extractor hoods. They filter the gasses from chemical "
"reactions and pump the cleaned air outside of the building."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 189
#: rc.cpp:1626
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Thermometer"
msgid "Contact Thermometer"
msgstr "থার্মোমিটার"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 190
#: rc.cpp:1629
msgid ""
"A contact thermometer is different from a regular thermometer because of its "
"sensor for the current temperature. Such a thermometer is connected with a "
"heating coild. If the sensor notices that the aimed temperature has been "
"reached the contact thermometer will make the heating coild stop heating. "
"Therefore in an experiment it is possible to have a constant temperature."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 194
#: rc.cpp:1632
msgid "Clamps"
msgstr "ক্ল্যাম্প"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 195
#: rc.cpp:1635
msgid ""
"With clamps as used in a laboratory you can easily hold all kinds of tools."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag name
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 199
#: rc.cpp:1638
msgid "Litmus Paper"
msgstr "লিটমাস কাগজ"

#. i18n: tag desc
#. i18n: file data/tools.xml line 200
#: rc.cpp:1641
msgid ""
"There are multiple way to measure the pH-Value of an solution. With a litmus "
"paper it is easy to get a pretty precise pH-Value. The color indicates the "
